Installation Guide              1993-01-10 (WED) Toru Aihara
==================
 
There are many ways to install WorkPlace objects. This guide shows
two simple examples I usually use.
 
(1) WP Class List
If you have toolkit, using WP Class List is the easiest way.
a) Put the DLL MBFOLDER.DLL into the directory which the LIBPATH
   in your CONFIG.SYS includes.
b) Open the WP Class List. Select 'Add a new class...' from the
   popup menu, and fill in the dialog box in the following way.
        New class name:    MbFolder
        Library module:    MBFOLDER.DLL
c) Select the class MbFolder you created in step b, and select
   'Create an instance...' from the popup menu, and fill in the
   dialog box to get an instance, a folder with a menu bar.
 
(2) REXX
a) Put the DLL MBFOLDER.DLL into the directory which the LIBPATH
   in your CONFIG.SYS includes.
b) Register the class.
   call RxFuncadd 'SysLoadFuncs','RexxUtil','SysLoadFuncs'
   cal  SysLoadFuncs
   RetCode = SySRegisterObjectClass("MbFolder","MBFOLDER")
c) Create an instance.
   RetCode = SysCreateObject("MbFolder","Menu Bar Folder","<WP_DESKTOP>")
